version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-25"
# Identifiers below are recorded AUTOMATICALLY on each release by
# .github/workflows/release-identifiers.yml — don't fill them in by hand.
#
# `doi:` is the CONCEPT DOI: it means "cite this project" and deliberately
# resolves to whatever version is latest. That floating behaviour is correct
# HERE and wrong in a nanopub — see scripts/set_release_identifiers.py.
#
# (This used to say "run /init-template again or edit by hand". /init-template
# deletes itself as its final step, so by the time a DOI existed the skill it
# named was gone and "edit by hand" was the only path left. Two repos built from
# this template then recorded the version DOI two different ways — one a
# structured identifier, one a prose comment. Hence the automation.)
# No `doi:` / `identifiers:` yet — the Zenodo concept DOI does not exist until
# the first release mints it. scripts/set_release_identifiers.py (via
# release-identifiers.yml) inserts them on release:
#   doi:          <concept DOI>
#   identifiers:  concept DOI + version DOI + Software Heritage ID
# A leftover DOI placeholder token here would ship a non-resolving DOI as a
# citable identifier, so it is intentionally absent rather than templated.
keywords:
  - replication
  - reproducibility
  - FORRT
  - nanopublication
  - Science-Live
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Deriving Water Quality Parameters Using Sentinel-2 Imagery: A Case Study in the Sado Estuary, Portugal"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Sent"
        given-names: "Giulia"
    year: "2021"
    doi: "10.3390/rs13051043"
